# Bug Report: Proof Breakdown in InnerProductProof System for RangeCheck

## Describe the Bug

The bug is found on [this branch](https://github.com/spaceandtimelabs/sxt-proof-of-sql/tree/feat/range-check-arbitrary-word-columns)

Go directly to the failing test [here](https://github.com/spaceandtimelabs/sxt-proof-of-sql/blob/bb7d8c8addafbbb906b6be199a5a2bf1e6b333da/crates/proof-of-sql/src/sql/proof_gadgets/range_check_test.rs#L329-L362)

The `InnerProductProof` system fails to verify a column of scalars when the range includes values up to `10241`, while the same proof system works correctly for ranges up to `10240`. Notably, the `DoryProof` system verifies the same range (`0..10241`) without any issues.

## To Reproduce
### Minimal Example
Here is a minimal test that reproduces the issue in the `InnerProductProof` system:

```rust
#[test]
fn ipa_proof_breaks_down_on_range_check() {
    // Create a column of scalars from 0 to 10240
    let data = owned_table::<Curve25519Scalar>([scalar("a", 0..10240)]);
    let t = "sxt.t".parse().unwrap();
    let accessor = OwnedTableTestAccessor::<InnerProductProof>::new_from_table(t, data, 0, ());
    let ast = RangeCheckTestPlan {
        column: ColumnRef::new(t, "a".into(), ColumnType::Scalar),
    };
    let verifiable_res = VerifiableQueryResult::<InnerProductProof>::new(&ast, &accessor, &());
    let res: Result<QueryData<MontScalar<ark_curve25519::FrConfig>>, QueryError> =
        verifiable_res.verify(&ast, &accessor, &());
    assert!(res.is_ok());

    // Now create a column of scalars from 0 to 10241
    let data = owned_table::<Curve25519Scalar>([scalar("a", 0..10241)]);
    let t = "sxt.t".parse().unwrap();
    let accessor = OwnedTableTestAccessor::<InnerProductProof>::new_from_table(t, data, 0, ());
    let ast = RangeCheckTestPlan {
        column: ColumnRef::new(t, "a".into(), ColumnType::Scalar),
    };
    let verifiable_res = VerifiableQueryResult::<InnerProductProof>::new(&ast, &accessor, &());
    let res: Result<QueryData<MontScalar<ark_curve25519::FrConfig>>, QueryError> =
        verifiable_res.verify(&ast, &accessor, &());

    if let Err(e) = res {
        panic!("Verification failed: {e}");
    }
}

```

